ervant of the dark  lord  disgusted with the actions of the  quote-unquote good guys and fueled by  the torment that he'd endured for much  of his upbringing snape turned to the  dark side and became one of voldemort's  right-hand men in fact it was snape  himself that overheard sybil trolloni  discussing the fabled prophecy and snape  2 who relayed the message to voldemort  the two were close snape trusted  voldemort and voldemort trusted snape  but that all changed when lily evans  life was in danger given that snape was  in voldemort's inner circle for so many  years and that he had formed such a  close bond with him i always wondered  was snape aware of voldemort's horcraxes  and if not why wasn't he snape was a  bonafide magical genius and he knew more  about magic than almost every other  wizard in the wizarding world having  gone down the rabbit hole of both sides  of the wizarding spectrum good and bad  not only that but he was a master  legilimens a master of the mind  he knew exactly how to read people how  to analyze their behaviors and patterns  how could he have missed powerful dark  magic at play the truth is snape didn't  know about voldemort horcruxes but it's  not because he wasn't observant or  because he did anything wrong he simply  missed them because he didn't know what  they were horcruxes are one of the  darkest forms of magic and the number of  witches wizards aware of their existence  is infinitesimal the only reason that  tom riddle was lucky enough to have  learned more about them is because horus  loghorn was his teacher who just so  happened to have some info about them in  fact slughorn's inadvertent guidance was  undoubtedly instrumental in voldemort's  rise to power though snape had delved  deep into the dark guards horcruxes  aren't exactly a common topic even in  the realm of dark magic that's how taboo  the subject is when hermione searches  for the books in the restricted section  none of them give details on horcruxes  and only 